    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1321">

                <pb facs="1044" n="928" xml:id="pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/20.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-29T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Some 2,000 Chinese at Cananea are likely to be attacked at any moment. Chinese
                    Chargé d’Affaires requests me to instruct our consular agent there to afford
                    protection. I told him that I could not act without instruction. Will the
                    Department instruct the consular agent and advise me in the sense of its
                    instruction?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
